  "question": {
    "text": "The distance between Sun and Earth is $R$. The duration of year if the distance between Sun and Earth becomes $3 R$ will be:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "krCou",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{3}$ years",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "sP5Qr",
      "text": "3 years",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Atsfr",
      "text": "9 years",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "dWiax",
      "text": "$3 \\sqrt{3}$ years",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Basically 1 year is equal to time period of earth revolution around sun.\nSo, $T_i=1$ year\nNow,\n$T^2 \\propto R^3$\n$\\therefore\\left(\\frac{T_2}{T_1}\\right)^2=\\left(\\frac{R_2}{R_1}\\right)^3$\n$\\Rightarrow T_2=\\left(\\frac{R_2}{R_1}\\right)^{3 / 2} T_1=\\left(\\frac{3 R}{R}\\right)^{3 / 2} \\times 1$\n$=3 \\sqrt{3}$ years.",
    "image": null
  },
